+s2 yields higher scores than Ratings5, with relative
+improvements of 8.24% in F1@10, 11.03% in MRR@1
+0, and 9.31% in NDCG@10. Therefore, neither thresh
+old is uniformly superior across all evaluation metric
+s, and the preferred setting depends on the recomme
+ndation cutoff and evaluation objective.
+According to Table 1, CiaoDVD has the lowest inter
