+Abstract  Existing
+Graph Signal Processing (GSP)-based recommender
+systems do not
+explicitly
+incorporate
+user
+ratings
+when
+constructing
+interaction
+graphs.
+We
+propose
+Rating-Aware
+Graph
+Filtering. The method independently filters interaction-based and rating-based adjacency matrices and
+combines their outputs through weighted aggregation. Experiments on ML-100K, ML-Latest-Small,
+ML-1M, and CiaoDVD evaluate F1, MRR, and NDCG using rating thresholds of 2 (Ratings2) and 5
+(Ratings5). Compared with HiGSP, Ratings2 improves 23 of 24 dataset-metric comparisons, while
+Ratings5 improves all 24. However, Ratings2 slightly decreases MRR@10 on ML-1M. These results
+indicate that user ratings can improve recommendation performance, although gains depend on the
+dataset, rating threshold, combination weights, and evaluation metric.
